Implement Istio resilience features covering rate limiting, circuit breaking, and fault injection for the svp platform.

files:
- k8s/istio/rate-limit.yaml
- k8s/istio/fault-injection.yaml

rate-limit.yaml:
EnvoyFilter resource, namespace svp.
name: customer-user-service-rate-limit.
apply to workloads with label app: customer-user-service.
use a LOCAL_RATE_LIMIT filter on the inbound HTTP filter chain.
set token bucket to 10 requests per second with a burst of 10.
return HTTP 429 when the limit is exceeded.

fault-injection.yaml:
two VirtualService patches, one for latency and one for abort.
do not replace the existing virtual-services.yaml, create separate resources.

VirtualService named customer-user-service-fault, namespace svp:
match on prefix /customers.
inject a 3 second delay on 50% of requests using httpFault.delay.
bind to no gateway, applies to mesh internal traffic only.
host: customer-user-service.

VirtualService named expense-service-fault, namespace svp:
match on prefix /expenses.
inject an HTTP 503 abort on 30% of requests using httpFault.abort.
bind to no gateway, applies to mesh internal traffic only.
host: expense-service.

imports / dependencies:
apiVersion networking.istio.io/v1beta1 for VirtualService.
apiVersion networking.istio.io/v1alpha3 for EnvoyFilter.
EnvoyFilter LOCAL_RATE_LIMIT uses the envoy.filters.http.local_ratelimit typed config.
fault injection VirtualServices apply to mesh traffic, not gateway traffic, so gateways field is omitted.
the existing destination-rules.yaml outlierDetection already provides passive circuit breaking.
these files are applied manually for testing and removed afterwards, not wired into install_istio.py.

standards:
follow kubernetes best practices.
use resource requests and limits on all containers.
add liveness and readiness probes where appropriate.